  "name": "Bard",
  "system": {
    "description": {
      "value": "<p><em>A bright tune to soothe a party's wounds... A brisk march to raise a party's spirits... A forbidden chant to weaken a party's foes... Bards use music as their weapon.</em></p><h2>Role</h2><p>The bard transcends mere entertainer, weaving the very essence of Aether and Melody into their craft to become the ultimate party support and master of social engineering. They are the quintessential force multipliers in combat, utilizing Charisma-based performances to empower allies with uplifting hymns, granting bonuses to attacks, defenses, or even mending wounds with soothing serenades. A melancholic dirge or discordant aria can sow confusion, fear, or vulnerability among foes, applying debilitating status effects like Silence, Sleep, or Slow.</p><h2>Class Skills</h2><p>The bard's class skills are Acrobatics (Dex), Appraise (Int), Bluff (Cha), Climb (Str), Craft (Int), Diplomacy (Cha), Disguise (Cha), Escape Artist (Dex), Intimidate (Cha), Knowledge (all) (Int), Linguistics (Int), Perception (Wis), Perform (Cha), Profession (Wis), Sense Motive (Wis), Sleight of Hand (Dex), Spellcraft (Int), Stealth (Dex), and Use Magic Device (Cha).</p><h2>Weapon and Armor Proficiency</h2><p>A bard is proficient with all simple weapons and harp bows. Bards are proficient with light armor but not with any shields. Because the somatic components required for bard songs are relatively simple, a bard can perform songs while wearing light armor without incurring the normal song failure chance. However, like mages, a bard wearing medium or heavy armor or using a shield incurs a chance of song failure.</p><h2>Main Ability Score</h2><p>The bard mainly focuses on Dexterity for martial combat and Charisma for their class features and songs.</p>",
      "instructions": ""
    },
